# Patch 0054 — scanout allocated from a 64 MiB no-map carveout instead of CMA.
#
#   echo 0054-arm64-dts-h713-EXPERIMENT-scanout-from-a-carveout.patch \
#       >> patches/kernel/series
#   KERNEL_CONFIG=carveout build/build.sh kernel
#     -> build/out/h713-kernel-carveout.fit
#
# 0054 is an EXPERIMENT and must not live in `series`: it changes where every
# scanout buffer comes from, and a plain `build/build.sh kernel` would ship it.
# Add the line, build, take it out again.
#
# Like dispiommu.config and nocache.config this fragment changes NO config
# symbol. It exists so the build gets its own tree and its own FIT name, and
# it deliberately leaves CONFIG_LOCALVERSION empty so `uname -r` stays 6.18.38
# and /lib/modules/6.18.38 -- including the out-of-tree aic8800 WiFi/BT modules
# -- still loads. That keeps the network up, which is what makes the run
# observable over ssh rather than over a 115200-baud console.
#
# CHECK IT TOOK, because a silent fallback to CMA would look exactly like a
# clean result and mean nothing:
#
#   dmesg | grep -i "DMA memory pool at 0x0000000070000000"
#   grep -c 70000000 /proc/iomem
#   grep CmaFree /proc/meminfo     # must stay ~flat while mpv runs
#
# That last one is the real gate. On the CMA arm CmaFree drops by about 18 MiB
# when mpv starts; if it still does, the pool was not used and the run is void.
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION=""
